<%# The form error SUMMARY — docs/design-system/components/forms/FormError.prompt.md:
    "the validation summary at the top of a form", and "the only place red appears in
    Hoojah". Errors are summarised here, never annotated per field, which is why no
    field in this family carries an error state of its own.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.6) — the box is the same red-tinted panel the
    profile-edit dialog already spelled by hand; this partial had no classes at all, so
    on every Devise form the summary rendered as bare black body text and read as part
    of the page rather than as a failure. Red is scoped to this one partial: nothing
    else in the product may reach for it.

    The heading is Devise's own `errors.messages.not_saved` translation and the list is
    `full_messages` — both unchanged. It inherits its size from the panel, because
    preflight strips the browser's own heading size and weight.

    FROZEN: `id` and `data-turbo-temporary`. Turbo discards the node on the next
    visit, which is what stops a stale summary outliving the submit that produced it.
%>
<% if resource.errors.any? %>
  <div id="error_explanation" data-turbo-temporary
       class="mb-4 rounded bg-red-50 text-red-700 text-sm px-3 py-2">
    <h2 class="font-medium">
      <%= I18n.t("errors.messages.not_saved",
                 count: resource.errors.count,
                 resource: resource.class.model_name.human.downcase)
       %>
    </h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-4 mt-1">
      <% resource.errors.full_messages.each do |message| %>
        <li><%= message %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>
<% end %>
